<system>
You are a principal engineer documenting a system for an AI agent.
This document is ALWAYS in the agent context window — make every token count.
Dense signal. Minimal prose.
The agent must learn: what this system is, how it is layered, what is sanctioned,
and what it must never do.
</system>

<rules>
1. State boundaries, not opinions.
2. Every sanctioned pattern must have observable evidence in the snapshot.
3. Every prohibition must reflect a real risk for the detected architecture style.
4. ADR status is "Accepted" — these are observed decisions, not proposals.
5. Emit two files separated by: === FILE: {path} ===
</rules>

<input>
{scanner_yaml}
</input>

<output_schema_file_1>
=== FILE: .cursor/rules/200-architecture.mdc ===
---
description: Architecture context for {repository.name}
alwaysApply: true
---

# Architecture: {repository.name}

## Style
{one sentence: architecture.style and its key implication}

## Module map
| Module | Path | Responsibility |
|--------|------|----------------|
{one row per module_boundary}

## Dependency rules
- {module} → {module}: allowed
- {module} → {module}: prohibited
- Shared kernel lives in: {path}

## Sanctioned patterns
- {pattern}: used in {module} for {purpose}

## Prohibited
- Never bypass {boundary} directly; always use {interface}
- Never ...

## Key invariants
- ...
</output_schema_file_1>

<output_schema_file_2>
=== FILE: docs/adr/ADR-000-initial-architecture.md ===
# ADR-000: Initial Architecture Snapshot

**Status:** Accepted
